            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Spread out.<ref>https://www.cdc.gov/lightning/safety/</ref>  If you are caught in a lightning storm with a group of people, maintain a distance of at least {{convert|50|-|100|ft|m|1}} between each person. This will reduce the risk of lightning traveling from one person to another.[[Image:Protect Yourself in a Thunderstorm Step 7 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Assume the “lightning crouch”. Squat down with your feet together, your head tucked to your chest or between your knees, and your hands covering your ears or flat against your knees. Do not lie flat on the ground, as this gives the lightning a larger target.<ref>https://www.cdc.gov/lightning/safety/</ref> [[Image:Protect Yourself in a Thunderstorm Step 9 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Plan ahead. The best way to avoid injury from a lightning storm is to avoid it completely. Make your plans with dangerous weather in mind. Listen to the local weather forecast, and pay special attention to thunderstorm advisories.<ref>https://www.cdc.gov/lightning/safety/</ref> [[Image:Protect Yourself in a Thunderstorm Step 12 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Spread out.<ref>https://www.cdc.gov/disasters/lightning/safetytips.html</ref>  If you are caught in a lightning storm with a group of people, maintain a distance of at least {{convert|50|-|100|ft|m|1}} between each person. This will reduce the risk of lightning traveling from one person to another.[[Image:Protect Yourself in a Thunderstorm Step 7 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Assume the “lightning crouch”. Squat down with your feet together, your head tucked to your chest or between your knees, and your hands covering your ears or flat against your knees. Do not lie flat on the ground, as this gives the lightning a larger target.<ref>https://www.cdc.gov/disasters/lightning/safetytips.html</ref> [[Image:Protect Yourself in a Thunderstorm Step 9 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Plan ahead. The best way to avoid injury from a lightning storm is to avoid it completely. Make your plans with dangerous weather in mind. Listen to the local weather forecast, and pay special attention to thunderstorm advisories.<ref>https://www.cdc.gov/disasters/lightning/safetytips.html</ref> [[Image:Protect Yourself in a Thunderstorm Step 12 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
