            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "{{fa}}Lightning is a beautiful and inspiring phenomenon, but it can be deadly. Over the past 30 years, lightning has killed an average of 67 people per year in the United States alone. Fortunately, most lightning-related deaths are preventable. Follow these steps to safety the next time there’s fire in the sky.",
                    "[[Category:Weather Safety]]",
                    "== Steps ==",
                    "=== Taking Shelter and Staying Safe ===",
                    "*Lightning does not only happen during thunderstorms; it can also happen during volcanic eruptions. So you should also know about volcano safety and lightning safety. The more ash there is the more likely lightning will strike.",
                    "__PARTS__"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "Lightning is a beautiful and inspiring phenomenon, but it can be deadly. Over the past 30 years, lightning has killed an average of 67 people per year in the United States alone. Fortunately, most lightninguhug-related deaths are preventable. Follow these steps to safety the next time there’s fire in the sky.",
                    "[[Category:Weather Safety]][[Media:Example.ogg]]",
