            "summary": "(RCP reverted edits by 71.45.58.18 (talk) to  revision #21715089 by Revisiongeek)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#* Substantial, frequently inhabited buildings (those grounded with plumbing, electrical systems, and, if possible, lightning rods) are best.",
                    "#* If you can’t find a substantial structure, get in a car with a metal roof and sides. If the car is struck, the metal body will conduct the electricity around you, not through you. Make sure all windows are rolled up and doors are closed. Be careful not to lean against any metal -- if you do, the lightning will be conducted into your body if it strikes the car. Do not use the radio."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#* Substantial, frequently inhabited buildings (those grounded with plumbing, electrical systems, and, if possible, lightning rods) are the worst things to have",
                    "#* If you can’t find a substantial structure, get in a car with a metal roof and sides. If the car is struck, the metal body will not conduct the electricity around you, and go through you. Make sure all windows are rolled up and doors are closed. Be careful not to lean against any metal -- if you do, the lightning will be conducted into your body if it strikes the car. Do not use the radio."
                ]
            }
        },
