            "reverted_by": "Joel.Miles925",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "{{fa}}[[Image:Thunderstorm over Chesapeake Bay 9534.jpg|thumb|Thunderstorm over the Chesapeake Bay near Washington, D.C.]]Lightning is a beautiful and inspiring phenomenon, but it can be deadly.  Over the past 30 years, lightning has killed an average of 67 people per year in the United States alone.  Fortunately, most lightning-related deaths are preventable.  Follow these steps to safety the next time there’s fire in the sky."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "{{fa}}[[Image:Thunderstorm over Chesapeake Bay 9534.jpg|thumb|Thunderstorm over Chesapeake Bay near Washington, D.C.]]Lightning is a beautiful and inspiring phenomenon, but it can be deadly.  Over the past 30 years, lightning has killed an average of 67 people per year in the United States alone.  Fortunately, most lightning-related deaths are preventable.  Follow these steps to safety the next time there’s fire in the sky."
                ]
            }
        },
        {
