            "id": "7961536",
            "user": "RpUral",
            "timestamp": "15:39, 21 June 2012",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(9,792 bytes)",
            "change": -7,
            "summary": "(Reverted edits by 2.96.127.202 (Talk); changed back to last version by Amw705)",
            "is_minor": true,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "reverted",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "reverted_by": "Isorhythmic",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#[[Image:173803899_6ee6a89e79.jpg|200px|right]] '''Understand what constitutes suitable shelter.''' The key to minimizing lightning danger is to get inside a protective structure. Substantial, frequently inhabited buildings (those grounded with plumbing, electrical systems, and, if possible, lightning rods) are best.  Small structures, such as stand alone public restrooms, are generally not good choices, and standing under a tree is a very bad choice.  If you can’t find a substantial structure, get in a car with a metal roof and sides:  if the car is struck, the metal body will conduct the electricity around you, not through you.  When you’re outside, determine where the nearest suitable structure is in advance so that you’ll be ready should you be caught in a lightning storm.."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#[[Image:173803899_6ee6a89e79.jpg|200px|right]] '''Understand what constitutes suitable shelter.''' The key to minimizing lightning danger is to get inside a protective structure. Substantial, frequently inhabited buildings (those grounded with plumbing, electrical systems, and, if possible, lightning rods) are best.  Small structures, such as stand alone public restrooms, are generally not good choices, and standing under a tree is a very bad choice.  If you can’t find a substantial structure,do not get in a car with a metal roof and sides:  if the car is struck, the metal body will conduct the electricity around you, and you will die.  When you’re outside, determine where the nearest suitable structure is in advance so that you’ll be ready should you be caught in a lightning storm.."
                ]
            }
        },
