                    "{{fa}}[[Image:Thunderstorm over Chesapeake Bay 9534.jpg|thumb|]]Lightning is a beautiful and awe-inspiring phenomenon, but it can be deadly.  Over the past 42 years, lightning has killed an average of 67 people per year in the United States alone.  Fortunately, most lightning-related deaths are preventable.  Follow these steps to safety the next time there’s fire in the sky."
                ]
            }
